          "passage": "Studies of the Effects of Tilling vs. No Tilling on Crop Yields\nAuthors Crop Crop yield with tilling\n(Kilograms per hectare)\nCrop yield with no tilling\n(Kilograms per hectare)\nBharat Sharma Achayara\nand colleagues soybeans 3,062 2,670\nAdrian Gracia-Romero\nand colleagues maize 2,420 2,990\nDaniel Jug\nand colleagues winter wheat 4,860 3,910\nMin Huang\nand colleagues rice 2,534 5,226\nDaniel Jug and colleagues found that\ntilling—the practice of turning soil with hoes,\nplows, or other machines before planting\ncrops—was associated with an increased yield of\nwinter wheat. But some studies of other crops\nhave found the opposite effect; for example,\n_______",
