          "passageTitle": "Command of Evidence - Graphs — Q71",
          "passage": "1980-81 2005-06\n0\n40\n80\n120\n160\n200\nDays\nDays per Winter That Lakes Have Surface Ice\nLake Baikal\nOrhlujärvi\nLake Kegonsa\nIt is common for freshwater lakes near or above\na latitude of 45° north of the equator, like Lake\nStechlin in Germany, to accumulate surface ice\nin winter. A study from 1980 to 2006 showed\nthat, in general, the number of days per winter\nthat such lakes have measurable amounts of\nsurface ice is declining. However, a researcher\nclaimed that some lakes have instead seen an\nincrease in the duration of ice, citing as an\nexample _____",
